From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:19:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] sycl : fewer launches in the MTP verify graph

Measured in the replayed verify graph of the qwen35 hybrid (27B, Q4_K_M,
40k context) on an Arc Pro B70: 42.8 ms at 2 tokens and 48.1 ms at 8,
of which the quantized matmuls take 33.7 / 36.2 ms and about 1700 small
kernels take 3.9 / 4.5 ms. Three env switches, default off, outputs
bit-identical, remove launches from that graph:
- GGML_SYCL_XMX_GATEUP=2: FFN gate and up (two q4_K weights of the same
  shape, 1..8 columns) run as one activation quantize and one direct
  XMX launch that also applies the SwiGLU (=1 keeps the GLU op;
  GGML_SYCL_XMX_GATEUP_CHECK compares with the separate ops)
- GGML_SYCL_CONV_STEP=1: the conv-state concat and its rollback snapshot
  copies run as one kernel; the conv + SiLU joins when its output
  shares no memory with the inputs, and a snapshot row that shares
  memory with an input or another snapshot keeps its own turn
  (GGML_SYCL_CONV_STEP_CHECK)
- GGML_SYCL_TOPK_BATCH=1: the per-row TOP_K nodes of the backend sampler
  run as one launch sequence for up to 16 rows (GGML_SYCL_TOPK_BATCH_CHECK)
Also GGML_SYCL_CPY_BATCH=1 (consecutive f32 copies in one launch; not
needed with CONV_STEP).

Verify graph 48.10 -> 46.92 ms at 8 tokens and 42.80 -> 42.04 ms at 2;
decode with a fixed seed +2.0..2.4% at 40k..80k context with the same
accepted and drafted token counts; KL against the stored reference
unchanged in every printed digit.

Diagnostics: GGML_SYCL_NODE_STAMP=N prints the GPU time per node group
of replayed graphs from in-graph clock stamps (_DUP runs each matmul /
attention a second time for the warm-cache time, _TAGONLY, _DUMP,
_FILE). test-hostv-reuse takes HOSTV_N_EMBD, HOSTV_N_FF and
HOSTV_QTYPE=q4_K; test-backend-ops gains TOPK_ROWS and the gate/up
shape.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
